<TEI xmlns="http://www.tei-c.org/ns/1.0">
  <teiHeader>
      <fileDesc>
         <titleStmt>
            <title>Mary Behrend's Calendar Sheets</title>
         </titleStmt>
         <publicationStmt>
            <p>Published by Penn State Behrend.</p>
         </publicationStmt>
         <sourceDesc>
            <p>Created by Mary Behrend in 1909 for her husband.</p>
         </sourceDesc>
      </fileDesc>
  </teiHeader>
  <text>
      <body>
         <figure>
            <head>
               MARCH 11, 1909<lb/>
               THURSDAY
            </head>
            <figDesc>Four feminine figures appear to be talking or arguing. They're each wearing differently colored clothes, from left
            to right, appearing as purple, red, blue, and green. The purple and red figures have appropriately colored flamoyant hats.
            Each woman has a red face, and the red and green woman are pointing at each other and yelling, implying an argument.</figDesc>
         </figure>
         <p>
         <l>Everybody dressed in their best</l>
         <l>For <hi rend="underlined">this</hi> is an <hi rend="underlined">Erie Tea</hi></l>
         <l>They <hi rend="underlined">eat</hi> too much, <hi rend="underlined">talk</hi> too much-</l>
         <l>You can bet they <gap reason="illegible" unit="word" quantity="2"></gap> in me.</l>
         <l><add place="left"><gap reason="illegible" unit="word" quantity="4"></gap> gay in Erie?</add></l>
      </p>
      </body>
  </text>
   
<!--I tried to play around with a paragraph of a continuous idea alongside the lines being broken up and marked.-->
<!--I think it works fine for the Thursday entry, but the Friday one appears a bit choppy because of it.-->
   
   <text>
      <body>
         <figure>
            <head>
               <l>MARCH 12, 1909</l>
               <l>FRIDAY</l>
            </head>
            <figDesc>A woman in snow gear appears to be strutting along in her snowshoes. Red dots appear around
            the edge of the snowshoes, seemingly connected with a thread or wire.</figDesc>
         </figure>
         <p>
            <l>Molly on</l>
            <l>snowshoes</l>
            <l>that Mr. Weir</l>
            <l>got.</l>
            <l>Pretty picture</l>
            <l>is it not?</l>
         </p>
         <p><add place="below">Love from <gap reason="illegible" unit="word" quantity="1"></gap></add></p>
      </body>
   </text>
</TEI>
